
48:player
129:Journey's End
130:Shen
131:I am Shen... one of the dragon clan.
132:When I was little, I was washed ashore by a storm. It was the master of Mahjong Soul Shrine who saved me.
133:The shrine master nursed me back to health, cared for me, and gave me a priceless gift...
134:This Sacred Tile. It's said to possess the miraculous power to turn fantasy into reality.
135:I was told that my journey was far from over.
137:And so, I set out.
138:True to those words, the world beyond held one new horizon after another.
139:Shen wove her memories into the fog, hoping to share them in vivid detail when she returned.
140:Though she journeyed alone, knowing someone was waiting for her kept her from ever feeling lonely.
141:And yet...
142:Huh?
143:Where... am I?
144:I was only gone for a mere few hundred years... Why has everything changed?
145:I'm... I'm back...
146:...Where are you?
147:No, you said you'd be here when I came back. We were supposed to share our stories...
148:This must be what humans call a dream. It can't be real.
149:I just need to sleep... Just a little nap, and everything will be fine when I wake up.
150:So, before she could make sense of the dull ache in her chest, she let her eyes drift shut.
151:Surely, when she opened them again, everything would be just as it was...
152:I don't know what happened after that.
153:Then you all barged in and tried to take my Sacred Tile...
154:It's a token of our promise! I won't let anyone take it!
155:Leia
156:I see. Her emotional distress during sleep must have caused both the Sacred Tile's power and her innate fog magic to spill out unchecked.
157:Even this very island might not actually exist...
158:How heartbreaking.
159:Yuzu
160:Argh... They say dragons live so long that a few centuries must feel like a blink to them.
161:Kaavi
162:But against the brief span of human fate, that blink is an eternity.
163:Considering our time with Lin Lang, that rings all too true.
165:So that person... my friend... is gone?
166:Her question plunges everyone into silence.
167:Ichihime
168:Oh no, nyaa... I don't know what to say anymore, nyaa...
169:Telling her the raw truth now might be too cruel.
171:...
173:No.
174:Frieren
175:Perhaps we could try THAT spell.
176:Everyone
177:Huh?
178:Looks like that special spell is our only shot right now.
179:Which one, nyaa...?
180:Ah! Could it be...?
181:Well then, here goes.
182:<color=#6CC2B6>Spell that creates wind, blossoms, snow, and moonlight out of thin air!</color>
183:A mahjong tile glowing with the same radiance as the Sacred Tile materializes in Frieren's hand.
184:The very spell found in the chest hidden deepest within the ruins – now cast for the first time.
185:Th-this is...?!
186:I remember this... It's...
187:That person used magic just like this back at the Shrine to teach me how to guide the fog...!
188:But no matter how hard I tried, I could never recreate it... So I hid it where no one could find it...
189:How can you...?
190:I wonder why, too.
191:I didn't expect my first attempt to yield such a wondrous result either.
192:Heh... Humans are just such selfish creatures, aren't they?
193:Even long after they're gone, they leave these peculiar marks carved deep into your memory.
194:???
195:It's fine if you can't master it right away. Take it with you on your journey.
196:The things you don't understand today will shine like beacons somewhere down the road.
197:String them together like pearls, and you might just discover a whole new perspective.
198:When that day comes, I know you'll be smiling.
199:Sniff...
200:Waaah–!!!
201:Liar.
202:That person used to tease the little dragon, saying a dragon's tears turned into valuable pearls.
203:But determined to prove herself mature and independent, she had never shed a single tear.
204:I told you... They don't turn into pearls... You liar.
205:Once Shen has calmed down, we begin packing up our makeshift camp.
206:With her lending a hand, the work goes much faster.
207:You can take the Sacred Tile with you.
209:Are you sure about this?
211:Isn't that what you treasure most?
212:Yeah... It was entrusted to me, but it ultimately belongs to the Shrine.
213:That person wouldn't want me to be a selfish child.
214:We can't blame you for what happened.
215:Though long-lived by human standards, she's still very much a child at heart.
216:None of the trouble she caused was born of malice, so there's no need to be too hard on her.
217:Actually, there's another reason.
218:{var:player_nickname}, could you be...?
219:No, that can't be right... Human lifespans are...
221:What is it?
222:N-nothing... I'm just overthinking things...
223:Even if the aura feels so familiar, it couldn't be...
224:For some reason, she shrinks back into a timid stance once more.
225:Anyway, I'll gather up all the fog. I won't cause any more trouble.
226:Without the mist disrupting mana, and with the Shrine's wish granted...
227:Madam Frieren and the others will be able to return to their world safely.
228:Madam, huh...
229:Hard to say there's anything wrong with that.
230:What about you after this?
231:After this... I'll probably carry on with my journey.
232:Won't you come visit the Shrine?
233:Yeah, who knows when we'll see each other again, nyaa!
234:Frie, you guys should stay over too, nyaa! As the priestess, I'll show you top-tier hospitality!
235:I'm... not ready yet.
236:Revisiting familiar places after everything has changed... I want to wait until I've grown enough to stand on my own – and can face it in my true form.
237:Maybe many years from now, I'll drop by for a visit. I'll be in your care then, Miss Ichihime.
238:Suddenly talking like a grown-up, nyaa!
239:Maybe this fog-formed body is simply unstable?
240:Well then, farewell, my friends.
241:...Safe journey.
242:To you as well.
243:Ichihime the Hero, the master witch and her apprentices, an innocent Demon King, and adventurers from another world –
244:Their shared story draws to a close here.
245:And afterward...
246:Fern
247:Mr. Stark, please stop trying to polish the tile in your hand.
248:It is not going to turn into a Dora.
249:Stark
250:Help me out, Frieren! I'm just a few points away from taking first place!
252:Hang on, {var:player_nickname} gave me an ancient grimoire that seems to record mystical magic...
253:As soon as I find the spell to turn all tiles into Red Five, I'll help you out.
254:No, actually... that's just a game log...
255:And so, after the adventure comes a return to peaceful, ordinary life.
256:...Or so it seems.
257:Deep within Mahjong Soul Shrine rests the treasured Sacred Tile.
258:From it, a wisp of fog tinged with a different hue quietly begins to seep out...
259:It was likely her familiar aura that the dragon sensed, causing it to manifest in her likeness before us.
260:That person asked me to carry the Sacred Tile, record everything I saw along the way, and come back someday so we could trade stories.
263:Use that spell of yours to make non-Dora tiles sparkle like gems or something!
